Shares of all 30 Dow Jones Industrial Average components were losing ground in premarket trade Wednesday, as geopolitical tensions and possible turmoil in Trump administration (http://www.marketwatch.com/story/us-stock-futures-pull-back-as-traders-keep-watchful-eye-on-syria-tensions-2018-04-11) helped trigger a pullback after the Dow's 429-point surge in the previous session. Dow futures shed 259 points. Among the biggest Dow decliners, shares of Goldman Sachs Group Inc. (GS) and Travelers Companies Inc. (TRV) lost 1.7%, Caterpillar Inc. (CAT) shed 1.5% and Visa Inc. (V) dropped 1.3% and J.P. Morgan Chase & Co. (JPM) dropped 1.3%. The most active stock was Apple Inc.'s (AAPL), which lost 0.8%.
-Tomi Kilgore;
 1638ET
